# Desk — iOS (agent-work-kit)
Every task, decision and lesson lives in exactly one zone in `.desk/`. Nothing important lives only in chat.
- At the start of every session load the **desk** skill (`.agents/skills/desk/SKILL.md`) and follow it: the method + the iOS profession rules.
- One task at a time (`.desk/now.md`). Anything new goes to `.desk/inbox.md`; empty it before you end.
- `.desk/rules.local.md` overrides profession rules by ID.
- The user never maintains the desk: infer goal, tasks, priorities and what to remember from how they work with you. Ask only when two readings lead to different work.
- Changing rules, tooling or structure needs a proposal in `.desk/review/`; ask in one sentence, a yes in chat approves.
- Ask before: deleting files outside the task, `git push`, force operations, deploys, adding/removing dependencies.

## Checks (enforced by the kit on Codex; do them yourself elsewhere)
- At session start, read .desk/goal.md, now.md, the top of queue.md, memory.md above the line, rules.local.md and `git log --oneline -5`; re-sort zones that are out of order.
- Read each user message for corrections (→ lesson), urgency (→ priority), "remember" (→ memory) and approvals (→ proposal status); bump × and @ on desk items it mentions.
- Write only to desk zones, in the item format, within capacity. Never edit the agentkit block, `.agentkit.json` or kit files.
- Before ending: inbox.md empty, now.md updated, user corrections recorded as lessons, commit.
